From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:33:37 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui, engine: office overlay adds uz-latn and uz-cyrl (interface and date names) when its catalogs are present

Adds uz-latn (Oʻzbekcha) and uz-cyrl (Ўзбекча) to the interface languages when the overlay
supplies their catalogs. ui-egui/build_office.rs looks for catalog-uz-latn.tsv and
catalog-uz-cyrl.tsv (written by `cargo xt i18n export`, fallback chain already applied) next to
overlay.env; when both exist the build gets cfg(office_uz), the catalogs are embedded with
include_str!, and LANGUAGES grows by two entries (plural_one_other, left to right). candidates()
maps `uz`, `uz-UZ` and `uz_UZ.UTF-8` to uz-latn and `uz_UZ@cyrillic` to uz-cyrl; Windows
`uz-Latn-UZ` and `uz-Cyrl-UZ` already resolve by script. The engine gets its own build.rs that reads
dates-uz-latn.tsv and dates-uz-cyrl.tsv (month and weekday names) into office_dates.rs, so
DATE_LANGUAGES stays equal to the interface languages (a test requires it). The picker name carries
the export's draft marker while Uzbek rows are unreviewed. Without the files the language lists
and their tests are upstream's.
